Source of motanka-fonts: the fonts upstream Omarchy v4.5.0 names in its
configuration that Ubuntu's archives do not have, under
/opt/motanka/share/fonts, for both suites (Architecture: all).

At present that is "JetBrainsMono Nerd Font" and "JetBrainsMono Nerd Font
Mono" from Nerd Fonts 3.5.1, Regular, Bold, Italic and Bold Italic: the
monospace family of Upstream's bar, menus and terminals
(default/fontconfig/conf.avail/50-omarchy.conf maps "monospace" to it, the
shell's Style.qml asks for "monospace", and config/alacritty,
config/ghostty and config/foot name it). Upstream's Arch package is
ttf-jetbrains-mono-nerd-basic; its PKGBUILD is not public, so the set is
chosen from the family and style names Upstream's files use. The archive's
other families (Propo and the NL variants without ligatures) and lighter or
heavier weights are left out: no Upstream file names them.
debian/fonts.list is the list. packages.yaml maps
ttf-jetbrains-mono-nerd-basic to this package, and motanka-core depends on
it through its debian/pkgmap-depends.

The upstream archive is listed in stack/fonts-components.tsv (imported by
build-imports); test/vm/build fetches it with stack/fetch-sources
--components stack/fonts-components.tsv. The archive may hold its files
without a top-level folder (build "files"): dpkg-source unpacks such a
component as it is, and debian/fonts-build.sh finds each listed font by
name at any depth. (packaging/build.sh unpacks components with
--strip-components=1 for its own copy, so for a flat archive dpkg-source -b
may warn "ignoring deletion of file"; the .dsc carries the archive
unchanged and the build in the chroot sees all of it.) The fonts ship
unchanged; the build checks each one's family, weight and slant with
fc-scan. The archive's OFL.txt is installed as
/usr/share/doc/motanka-fonts/OFL.txt; debian/copyright points to it.

Other sessions do not see these fonts (requirement 5.10): no fontconfig
file of the system lists /opt/motanka/share/fonts. Only the Motanka session
does. Its launcher sets FONTCONFIG_PATH=/opt/motanka/share/motanka/fontconfig,
where motanka-core's fonts.conf adds /opt/motanka/share/fonts, includes
Upstream's 50-omarchy.conf and then the system's /etc/fonts/fonts.conf
(design.md, "Session findings (fonts and default theme)"). So no fontconfig
cache is built at install time; each user's first Motanka session caches
the folder in ~/.cache/fontconfig.
